package "main"

// XFAIL (VM + native) — tracked in claude-todo.md.
//
// A float64 literal with many significant digits that sits JUST ABOVE a binary
// rounding tie must round to nearest-even (UP).  The shared integer-only
// converter common.ParseFloatLitToBits holds the significand in a 128-bit
// window and collapses everything below it into a single sticky flag, so for
// ~38+ significant digits just above a tie it loses the exact round bit and
// rounds DOWN — one ULP low.  LLVM (its own strtod) is correct, so this PASSES
// on the C/LLVM modes and FAILS on the VM modes (and would on native, which
// shares the converter).
//
// 1.0000000000000001110223024625156540424 -> nearest double is 1.0 + 1 ULP =
// 0x3FF0000000000001 = 4607182418800017409; the converter yields
// 0x3FF0000000000000 = 4607182418800017408.
//
// Proper fix: exact rounding via pkg/std/math/big once stdlib is bundled with
// the BUILDER (and strconv gains ParseFloat).  See claude-todo.md.
func main() {
	println(bit_cast(int64, 1.0000000000000001110223024625156540424))
}
